  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "QKhjj5ii6MC+xKBs2pOPhJYwBaw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:48:33.387Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Three access paths, and knowing which one exists where saves a wrong turn:\n\n- **On the reactor module** \u2014 `documentModelRegistry: IDocumentModelRegistry`, present on **both in-process and worker-backed** reactors. This is the server-side path.\n- **In the browser** \u2014 `useModelRegistry()` from `@powerhousedao/reactor-browser`, typed `IDocumentModelRegistry | undefined`. It returns **`undefined` until the reactor client module is set on the PH global**, so the result must be guarded before any method call.\n- **Through `IReactor`** \u2014 not available. The core interface does **not** expose the registry directly; to list model data through the reactor use `reactor.getDocumentModels(namespace?, paging?, signal?)`, which reads `getAllModules()` internally and filters by document-type prefix.\n\nThe asymmetry is worth internalising: registry *methods* (upgrade paths, single-step reducers, module lookup) need the registry object, while a *listing* of installed models is available from the reactor itself with paging and a namespace filter. Reaching for the registry to enumerate models on the server is the long way round.\n\n## Provenance\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/06-DocumentModelRegistry.md` \u2014 Accessing the registry\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:48:33.387Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:48:33.387Z"
    }
  },
  {
